<<~ ahu #/inscription>>
! Art Sigils — Example Zero Inscription

The image-facing Inscription occupies **900 characters**. Copy only the `<<~ art ...>>` invocation below, without the wrapper. Named `key="value"` parameters carry artistic direction; the 1,024-character target measures the invocation alone.

**Procedure authority (outside the transmitted artwork):** `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/procedures` — [[Art Sigils Procedure Grammar|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/procedures]], defining the house `~art` procedure and defaults. A Lares-enabled wiki needs its sigil binding; an image receiver may interpret the invocation directly.

```tiddlywiki
<<~ art worktype="messy concept-art board" subject="shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra" read="plan-oblique fantasy terrain promises passage; rival field studies dispute it" imagery="dominant regional relief: green lowlands, ochre ridges, snow heights; route vellum; dark Phlegra relic; embodied travelers; green refuge; cyan, amber, violet anomalies" treatment="Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Heinrich Berann panorama; cold-press watercolor and hypsometric tints; Luka Rejec mythpunk; Piranesi/Ian Miller charcoal; graphite, Bristol ink, gouache" composition="luminous regional panorama above uneven pinned studies on visibly different papers; broad sky, dark counterweight" relation="painted red high pass ends at cliff; white line corrects by lower saddle; bone or machine?; lived-in refuge disputes desolation" depiction-scope="board fills frame; figures inside studies">>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/literal-rendering>>
!! Literal rendering — reference prose

The following reference prose follows the `~art` declaration in the Procedures meme. It records expected substitution, not proof of live Lararium execution.

!!! A. Example Zero invocation

```text
messy concept-art board: shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra. Read: plan-oblique fantasy terrain promises passage; rival field studies dispute it. Imagery: dominant regional relief: green lowlands, ochre ridges, snow heights; route vellum; dark Phlegra relic; embodied travelers; green refuge; cyan, amber, violet anomalies. Treatment: Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Heinrich Berann panorama; cold-press watercolor and hypsometric tints; Luka Rejec mythpunk; Piranesi/Ian Miller charcoal; graphite, Bristol ink, gouache. Composition: luminous regional panorama above uneven pinned studies on visibly different papers; broad sky, dark counterweight. Relation: painted red high pass ends at cliff; white line corrects by lower saddle; bone or machine?; lived-in refuge disputes desolation. Depiction scope: board fills frame; figures inside studies.
```

All eight values appear explicitly, so the declaration's optional defaults do not enter this expansion.

!!! B. Delegated defaults

```tiddlywiki
<<~ art subject="a distant coast" read="the unseen seems near">>
```

```text
artwork: a distant coast. Read: the unseen seems near. Imagery: follow subject and read. Treatment: suit the read. Composition: serve the read. Relation: where meaningful. Depiction scope: follow worktype and imagery.
```

Here the shared Procedures definition supplies omitted `worktype`, `imagery`, `treatment`, `composition`, `relation`, and `depiction-scope` values.

!!! C. Interpretation boundary

The invocation alone can guide an image model without guaranteeing behavior. Exact house rendering requires the Lares sigil binding and procedure in scope; visual fidelity, geography and provenance need separate evidence.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bounds>>
!! Reading and depiction

* **Primary image:** a dominant, luminous plan-oblique relief landscape connects green lowlands, ochre ridges and snowy heights, through Patterson/Jenny shaded-relief influences and Berann panoramic organization.
* **Competing witnesses:** the high pass painted in red ends against a cliff; a white revised route takes a lower saddle. Phlegra charcoal invites contradictory skeletal and mechanical readings; a modest green refuge resists total desolation. Small color scraps retain unidentified cyan, amber and violet appearances.
* **Distinct materials:** cold-press watercolor, graphite on translucent vellum, charcoal on cool fibrous paper, ink on smooth Bristol and small gouache studies retain separate surface behaviors.
* **Depiction boundary:** the flat pinned board fills the frame. Artist, photographer, studio furniture, source photos, names and credits do not become depicted participants by virtue of their references.
* **Folio companion:** `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/art-sigils/example-zero-folio` — [[Example Zero Folio|ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/art-sigils/example-zero-folio]]. It carries expanded artistic sigils, visual arguments, specialized sources and their three real Olympus URIs.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>
!! Aftermath — two expressions, one artistic invitation

The compact invocation names the primary visual intention; the accompanying Folio expands distinct questions, material behaviors, viewpoints and sources. Source URLs and artist names guide visual interpretation but need not enter the rendered picture as labels. Neither the invocation nor its prose expansion certifies traversability, relic identity or fictional canon.
<<~/ahu>>

